# Two DIFFERENT comparisons. Confusing them has already produced a false claim
# that Studio was Neo-identical, so both are recorded with what each proves.
#
# neo_upstream_left_right: the local `neo` TRACKING branch against upstream/neo.
#   0 0 means the tracking branch has not drifted. It says NOTHING about the
#   product branch.
# neo_head_left_right: the tracking branch against the product HEAD. This is
#   the real divergence, and it is not small.
neo_upstream_left_right=0 0
neo_head_left_right=0 324
# ...measured at THIS commit, not at HEAD. Every commit advances the right-hand
# number, so a value pinned to a moving HEAD invalidates itself immediately --
# the test that checks this field failed on the very next commit when it was
# first written that way. Pinned to a named commit it stays verifiable forever.
neo_head_left_right_at=91c04492
neo_comparisons_checked=2026-08-18

# What that divergence consists of, in Neo-owned files: the files under
# modules/, modules_forge/ and backend/ counted below, catalogued as FOUR patch
# families in docs/14_PATCH_INVENTORY.md. ldm_patched/ and extensions-builtin/
# are untouched. Until 2026-10-19 backend/ was untouched too; PATCH-004 adds
# a model family Neo does not have (MOSS-Image) as NEW backend files, and the
# only existing backend files it edits are the loader's dispatch and the
# bundled-tokenizer table -- so no EXISTING family's inference, sampling or
# memory-management file is patched. Everything else in the 324 is
# Studio-owned code that did not exist in Neo.
#
# 2026-10-20, PATCH-005: one UPSTREAM backport, Neo's own `bd1d015` (Anima
# Control-LLLite block mapping), in backend/nn/anima.py and two
# extensions-builtin/sd_forge_controlllite files. Upstream's code, not
# Studio's; it leaves on the next sync.
#
# 2026-10-20, PATCH-006: one line in backend/sampling/sampling_function.py
# (`get_area_and_mult`'s mask repeat), so regional masks work on video-shaped
# latents (Anima). For every image latent it builds the same tensor as
# before (proved in tests/studio_alpha/test_rg1_regional.py), which is why
# `neo_inference_paths_modified` below is 1 and not 0: the sampler file is
# edited even though no image changes.
#
# Read `neo_inference_paths_modified` narrowly; until PATCH-006 it was 0. It means the DIFFUSION path
# is unpatched, and that is still true. It does NOT mean no Neo compute
# behaviour is patched: PATCH-003 changes upscale pixel handling and is the one
# place Neo-owned code imports forge_headless. Until 2026-08-18 this block said
# 15 files and two families, and described every patch as import-graph or
# install-time. That was three days out of date and wrong about the third
# family. Every number here is now recomputed from git by
# tests/studio_alpha/test_patch_inventory.py rather than transcribed by hand.
neo_owned_files_modified=39
neo_inference_paths_modified=1
neo_pixel_paths_modified=2

